{"author":{"id":"8022379585b4ab99ca8775db3eb67d33fcb256817114c28e51ccc1e9f55cdec4"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1791223597,"nonce":"7yPQcw2OUBO9Ou0Jjzy0bOHgc9I=","message":"Root cause: startup hooks run in the MIR interpreter while nothing is native yet; __vtable_init__ passes closure records (fn_ref bitcast to *u8) to haxe_closure_register_entries, whose ptr parameter the interpreter cannot marshal a Function value into ('Cannot convert Function(..) to usize'), so every tiered iteration failed instantly. Fix: the interpreter skips haxe_closure_register_entries and haxe_register_method; the native tier replays __vtable_init__ at tier-up and registers the real records. The runner's promotion wait now returns the iteration's error instead of the generic never-promoted message. knucleotide tiered: 609-621 ms on the nuc (llvm 546).","files":null}]}